  "question": {
    "text": "<p>In a Young's double slit experiment, the slit separation <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></math> is <math><mn>0.3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> and the screen distance <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></math> is <math><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>.</mo></math> A parallel beam of light of wavelength <math><mn>600</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> is incident on the slits at angle <math><mi>α</mi></math> as shown in figure. On the screen, the point <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math> is equidistant from the slits and distance <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math> is <math><mn>11.0</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>.</mo></math> Which of the following statement(s) is/are correct?<br ><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/45b41541-0720-460f-85e8-7343f8070828-image18.png\"/></p>",
